we met once and then twice back to back  two dates in london  and then it was i think about  three maybe four weeks later that i  managed to  persuade her to come and join me in  botswana  and we and we we camped out with each  other under the stars  now several years later we're learning  intimate new details about prince harry  and meghan markle's  romantic trips to botswana and how they  fell  in love what was fascinating was just  how quickly things developed and  those beautiful trips to botswana which  were able to retrace within the book and  of course  that second trip to botswana that was  where harry had  first spoken to megan about making his  wife that's finding freedom co-author  omit scooby revealing the moment harry  told megan  she was the one et's michelle turner sat  down with scobee  the day before the book's official  release on august 11.  you worked with harry and megan or did  they give permission for people close to  them  to speak harry and megan didn't take  part in the process of this book or  contribute any interviews but many of  the friends that we approached to speak  to to tell  aside a different side of the story were  so frustrated with some of the coverage  they had seen of their friends  they felt that the people they were  seeing on these pages were not their  friends  not the people that they knew and thanks  to those sources  we're learning what really happened when  harry met  megan it's really interesting that those  um trips to africa were really kind of  the linchpin  significant moments in their  relationship  i think that harry taking megan to  botswana and parts of africa and seeing  how she handled that  being okay sort of out on safari with  just a tent and  i remember saying that she was happy  just to take a pack of baby wipes  uh to clean her face and a backpack very  low  when it came to sort of what she was  what she needed to get through the day  she was sort of happy to wander off  into the forest for a bathroom break  those are the things that i think harry  would have noticed immediately that this  girl  was very much sort of on his level and  what he was about they shared a  substance with each other and  both the love for that same part of the  world as well which has  really united them we spent coming  joining for five days out there which  was absolutely fantastic so  then we were really by ourselves which  was crucial  to me to make sure that we had a chance  to get to know each other  of course there were the critics that  think harry moved too  fast  popping the question to megan a year and  a half after they first met  i don't think that i would call it a  whirlwind uh in terms of our  relationship  my heart swoons at the fact that three  months in  they were saying i love you and in  africa was one of the first times that  happened  my head is saying that's quick that's  really quick  listen harry and megan had both  experienced love  and proper relationships earlier on in  their lives megan of course had been  married before  she knew exactly what it is that would  work and what wouldn't work in a  relationship for her and i think harry  came to the table  with very much that same feeling and so  when they did meet  they did tick all the right boxes with  each other and the connection was strong  it made every sense to move forward from  that and not to look back and i think  while some people  accused them of rushing or thinking that  it was moving too fast  these were two adults well into their  30s that were also aware of the clock  ticking you know they wanted to settle  down and  have a family and i think it just made  perfect sense for it to follow  the path that it eventually did it's no  secret harry's older brother prince  william was one of the biggest critics  there's an important moment in the book  where william sits down with harry  to sort of express some of his own  concerns about the speed at which the  relationship was moving now  that's great brotherly advice and  especially if it was  asked for um but what we have to  remember in the build-up to that that  harry was already aware of some of the  things that were being said about megan  within the institution  he was already aware of some of the  disparaging comments that being made  behind his back by  some of his own friendship circle and so  when william came to him with this  conversation  i can see how it may have come across as  yet another unsupportive individual  at a time when he needed someone to have  his back so you can see how  things may have sort of changed from  that point onwards and  i have heard from sources close to  william that he very much regrets  having that conversation but despite  their differences  scoby is adamant that the brothers  relationship is  on the mend i think it's we make it very  clear in the book that you know  harry had a conversation with a friend  earlier this year  he spoke about the importance of that  bond of brotherhood and how that will  never  disappear from him so whilst we do see  two brothers now  spending time away from each other i  wouldn't call that the end of their  relationship i think that these things  sort of come in waves and  as harry said himself in that interview  in southern africa  that they don't see each other that  often but they're also on very different  paths and i think that those paths will  reconnect them at some point but  it is difficult
 

